        {
            "num": 3,
            "title": "List of materials and photo reference",
            "demo": true,
            "avo_lesson_id": 1444,
            "materials": [],
            "html_body": "<div class=\"materials-sheet\">\r\n<p class=\"materials-intro\">Materials Elke Memmler uses for the flower painting in this course.</p>\r\n<ol class=\"materials-items\">\r\n<li><strong>Paper.</strong> Elke always uses the big format 56 × 76 Fabriano or HAHNEMUHLE, 600–640 gr. The surface of the paper is heavily glued, smooth and satin, so the paint stays on the surface for a long time and only gradually penetrates into the lower layers, which gives time to react.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Brushes.</strong> Elke as a rule uses 5 brushes, both synthetic and natural:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The thickest round brush with a thin tip (synthetic) by Elke Memmler — German brand Lineum, released on special order</li>\r\n<li>Thick round brush protein (stores a lot of water and paint)</li>\r\n<li>Medium round squirrel brush, Kolinsky</li>\r\n<li>Thin round school brush (for drawing details)</li>\r\n<li>Fleyts (soft)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><strong>Paints.</strong> Elke uses paints by the South Korean firm MIJELLO. She does not highlight preferred colors and uses the versatility of the full palette.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Special blend.</strong> For the landscape, Elke used a mixture she made herself: titanium white and neapolitan yellow, water and some alcohol. It is used to draw trees and create a veil on the picture.</li>\r\n<li><strong>White mascara.</strong></li>\r\n<li><strong>Palette.</strong> Elke uses a large plastic palette (sized for thick brushes). It is divided into three parts: yellow and red shades; cold blues and greens; warm browns and greens.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Pencil.</strong> Elke usually does not use a simple pencil, as she does not create sketches. If required, she recommends any soft pencil to avoid damaging the paper.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Spray with water.</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<div class=\"reference-panel\">\r\n<h3>Photo reference</h3>\r\n<p>Reference photo Elke used as the basis for this work.</p>\r\n<div class=\"reference-media\"><img src=\"/assets/courses/elke-en/flower-reference.jpg\" alt=\"Flower reference photo\"></div>\r\n<a class=\"reference-download\" href=\"/assets/courses/elke-en/flower-reference.jpg\" download=\"elke-memmler_pions.jpg\">Download reference image</a>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>"
        },
